      "writtenOn": "2022-10-13T17:05:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When you move the setup before the loop, each iteration shares the same mount in the guest, and the guest won\u0027t need to re-fetch the file from the host after the first read.\n\nWe want to keep the setup inside the loop, i.e. in the VM we always remount a new filesystem instance to test against.  The cache I was talking about is the host\u0027s, i.e. what fd_server reads from.\n\nRe drop_caches: dropping cache in the guest is only necessary with the same mount in the guest (IIUC from the previous comment), but in this case we\u0027re talking about the host.",
